@title Final Fantasy Tactics Advance (USA)
@file Final Fantasy Tactics Advance (U) [!].gba
@game AFXE
@chip FLASH512
@status wip: reaches the snowball-fight tutorial battle at St. Ivalice (after naming Marche); mashing A does not advance the battle (the turn waits on a real command), and the first chance to save is the world map in Ivalice after this battle, the dream sequence and the first clan battle. A human should record: New Game, keep "Marche", play the snowball fight and the first battles, then Save on the world map and quit after the save message. [load]: title > SAVED GAME (Continue) > the slot > world map.

# Title > NEW GAME > A through the school scenes > name entry (START, then
# LEFT to Yes on "Confirm action. OK?", which defaults to No) > the snowball
# fight begins.

[new]
wait 600
mash START until text "NEW GAME" timeout=3000 every=60
wait 60
checkpoint title
press A
mash A until text "Name" timeout=6000 every=40
mash A until text "Enter" timeout=3000 every=40
wait 30
checkpoint name_entry
press START
until text "Confirm" timeout=300 every=5
wait 30
press LEFT after=20
press A after=60
